    {
      "severity": "FAIL",
      "title": "Public member lists are truncated without navigation",
      "description": "The route fetches only one page through `findMembers()`, which now defaults to 50 members. However, `app/assets/javascripts/discourse/templates/group/members.hbs` provides neither pagination controls nor incremental loading. Consequently, members beyond the first 50 are inaccessible from the public group page; previously, custom groups returned their complete membership. Add public pagination or incremental loading, with coverage for a group exceeding 50 members.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "correctness",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "app/assets/javascripts/discourse/routes/group-members.js.es6:8-11"
    },
    {
      "severity": "FAIL",
      "title": "Removing a member leaves their primary group assigned",
      "description": "The new removal endpoint deletes the membership through `group.users.delete(user_id)` but never clears a matching `User.primary_group_id`. The previous username-based removal path explicitly performed that cleanup in `Group#destroy_deletions`.\n\nA removed user can therefore retain the group as their primary group, and `PostSerializer#primary_group_name` continues displaying that affiliation. Clear the primary-group assignment when it matches the removed group, and add a regression test covering both membership removal and primary-group cleanup.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "correctness",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "app/controllers/admin/groups_controller.rb:90"
    },
    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Exact multiples of the page size produce an empty extra page",
      "description": "`Math.floor(user_count / limit) + 1` overcounts pages whenever the member count is an exact multiple of the limit. With 50 members and a limit of 50, the interface reports two pages and enables Next, which requests offset 50 and displays an empty list.\n\nUse `Math.ceil(user_count / limit)` and test counts of zero, exactly one page, and one page plus one member.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "correctness",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "app/assets/javascripts/admin/controllers/admin-group.js.es6:11-14"
    }
  ],
